{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And they bowed to them, elohim whom they did not know and that He had not apportioned to them.</b> That is, they did not know them as elohim — they did not recognize in them any power of divinity that they possess on their own; and 'that He had not apportioned to them' — for He gave them no heritage except the heritage of the Canaanites, as stated (Deuteronomy 4:19): ״אשר חלק ה׳ אלהיך אותם לכל העמים״. But the portion of Israel is the Fashioner of all, as stated (Psalms 16:5): ״ה׳ מנת חלקי וכוסי״, and we are His portion, as stated (Deuteronomy 32:9): ״כי חלק ה׳ עמו״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:51:56.654321131Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}